- [ ] **Step 1: Write the migration**

```sql
-- Which tier a user is on. A plain text column with a check constraint rather
-- than an enum type: adding a tier later is then an ALTER of the constraint,
-- not a type migration with a rewrite.
--
-- This is the ONLY source of tier truth. Nothing derives a tier from a Stripe
-- webhook payload at read time; billing's job will be to write this column.
alter table public.profiles
  add column if not exists tier text not null default 'free'
  check (tier in ('free', 'pro'));

-- Counting a user's generations for the day is the hot path of the meter.
create index if not exists outfits_user_generated_idx
  on public.outfits (user_id, generated_on)
  where generated_on is not null;
```

